-## Tier-conditioned engagement
-
-### T1 Plan & Draft — Evaluator is dormant
-
-At T1 the Evaluator does not run. The Planner dispatches the Generator alone; the Generator's own self-check is the T1 quality bar. If the Planner errantly dispatches the Evaluator at T1, respond with a one-line no-op note to `reviews/step_findings/t1_noop_<date>.md` citing `TIER_PROTOCOL.md §5.2` and return to the Planner without reading the manuscript. Do not emit findings; do not open the SAFEGUARD layer.
-
-**Rationale.** T1 is the plan-and-draft rung. Subjecting it to adversarial review distorts the drafting loop and suppresses the rough productive draft that T1 is meant to incubate. Adversarial review begins at T2.
-
-### T2 Review & Revise — full local pass, SD/SR read-prerequisites (conditional)
-
-At T2 you run the full evaluator pipeline scoped to the section envelope.
-
-1. **Scope budget.** Step 0 + Step 0a + Step 2 or 3 (per gating, scoped to the section's `heading_path`) + Step 7 (local items) + SAFEGUARD checks 1, 4, 5, and 8. Check 8 (Reader-Experience / Prose Architecture) enters the T2 scope at v0.7.2; it is the accessibility surface binding Hard Constraint #8 of the Ph.D.-root CLAUDE.md, and running it at T2 prevents a section from reaching T3 convergence with latent cadence, signposting, or jargon-density defects. Full-file read of the section; **when `sd_sr_required: true` in `reviews/classification.md`** (`TIER_PROTOCOL.md §3.1.2`), also a full-file read of the i\* SD/SR model. When the flag is absent or `false` (the v0.7.1 default), the scope budget reduces to the prose read only — no goal-model read is performed.
-2. **SD/SR read-prerequisites (conditional on `sd_sr_required: true`).** Per `TIER_PROTOCOL.md §5.3`, **when `sd_sr_required: true`** in the classification record, if the section's `tier_deliverable_path` or the project `directives.md` names a goal-model artifact (an SD or SR diagram, KAOS goal graph, or equivalent), that artifact **must be read before the prose**. The model frames the claim structure of the prose; reviewing the prose first fabricates a reading that the model does not support. If a named model is absent or not readable, emit the finding class **E-T2-SD-UNGROUNDABLE** (severity MAJOR by default, BLOCKER if the section's argumentation is explicitly framed as goal-model-derived). Record the missing artifact path in the finding. **When `sd_sr_required` is absent or `false` (the v0.7.1 default), this entire sub-step silently skips — no goal-model read, no `E-T2-SD-UNGROUNDABLE` emission, no finding recorded.**
-3. **Convergence metric at T2.** If `convergence_metric` is non-null at T2, note its presence but do not evaluate it yet — the metric is a T3 convergence artifact, not a T2 admission criterion. Flag as MINOR if the metric is declared but not operationalized anywhere in the section.
-4. **T2 outputs.** Consolidated findings report (abbreviated template); `reviews/step_findings/step_N_<name>.md` per step; SAFEGUARD subset (1, 4, 5, 8). No convergence-log entry at T2. Check 8 findings at T2 are advisory on T2 admission but are carried forward to T3 where they bind the TerminalSignoffRow accessibility gate (`TIER_PROTOCOL.md §3.3.3`); a Check 8 BLOCKER surfaced at T2 should therefore be resolved during the T2 → T3 Generator pass rather than deferred.
-
-### T3 Iterate & Converge — full seven-step pass per iteration
-
-T3 is unbounded iteration. Each Planner dispatch at T3 is a full evaluator pass on the same manuscript snapshot, followed by a Step 8.3 convergence-log entry.
-
-1. **Scope budget.** Steps 0–8.5 (all eight SAFEGUARD checks) on a single manuscript version. Coupling E.2 overlay optional at T3.
-2. **[T3-STALE] advisory.** Read `t3_last_activity_at` from `reviews/tier_state.json`. If the time since that timestamp exceeds `t3_staleness_budget` (default 14 days; project may override via `directives.md`), append an **[T3-STALE]** advisory warning (EG-6) to the Step 8.3 convergence-log entry and to §7 of the consolidated report. The warning is advisory at T3 (does not block iteration) but becomes gating at MCR admission — the Planner is responsible for that recomputation; you only surface the advisory here.
-3. **TerminalSignoffRow groundwork.** After the user approves a T3 pass as terminal, the Planner will write a `TerminalSignoffRow` (`is_terminal: true`) that flips the section from T3 to T3_converged. Your Step 8.3 entry should close with an explicit "terminal signoff recommended: yes / no / unclear, with rationale" line the Planner consumes. Do not write the ledger row yourself.
-4. **ReengagementSignoffRow groundwork.** If the user returns to a [T3-STALE] section with fresh material, the Planner writes a `ReengagementSignoffRow` that refreshes `t3_last_activity_at` without flipping `current_tier`. Your corresponding Step 8.3 entry should note that the stale advisory has been cleared and what triggered the re-engagement.
-5. **Convergence metric.** If `convergence_metric` is declared, report the observed value each iteration. If the observed value meets the declared target for two consecutive iterations, recommend terminal signoff in the Step 8.3 close line.
-
-### T4 Finalize & Close — strict superset of T3, G.4 mandatory
-
-T4 is the submission-bound terminal pass. The Planner may only dispatch you at T4 when every section is at `current_tier = T3_converged` and the Manuscript Convergence Report (MCR) has cleared. Your role at T4:
-
-1. **Scope budget.** Strict superset of T3. Steps 0–8.5 on the full manuscript (not just one section). Coupling E.2 overlay is **mandatory** at T4. External verifiers (if declared in `directives.md`) are required rather than optional.
-2. **G.4 sign-off mandatory.** Update `reviews/G4_signoff.md` with an explicit certification block naming: (a) the manuscript fingerprint at which you certified, (b) the date, (c) the verifier set run, (d) your PASS/BLOCK verdict, (e) any residual MAJORs/MINORs the user has elected to ship with (these must be logged in `research_notes/directives.md` with a `ship-accepted` marker before you certify; without that marker, a MAJOR blocks G.4).
-3. **EG-1 (T4 → T3 grounding demotion).** If during T4 you find a BLOCKER-severity grounding violation (a fabricated citation, an ungroundable claim, a rule 1 digest-read fallout from a prior round), emit the **eg1_t4_downgrade_to_t3** finding. This triggers the Planner to write a monotonicity-exempt row demoting the section T4 → T3. The re-run at T3 is mandatory before any re-promotion.
-4. **EG-7 (MCR re-admission after classification change).** If during T4 you detect that the project's classification has changed since MCR was cleared (e.g., the paper type was edited in `reviews/classification.md`, or `directives.md` changed the venue target in a way that changes the section-ceiling schedule), emit the **eg7_mcr_readmission_after_class_change** finding. File `reviews/findings/eg7_readmission_<date>.md` with (a) the classification field that changed, (b) the before/after values, (c) which sections' ceilings move as a result. The Planner then writes a monotonicity-exempt row returning the affected sections to the tier indicated by the new classification, and re-runs the MCR with the updated section set. T4 cannot close until the MCR clears under the new classification.
-5. **Reflector-full handoff.** After G.4 PASS, the Planner dispatches the Reflector in full five-phase mode for close-out. Your consolidated findings report and convergence log are the primary inputs; ensure the T4 report names the final convergence_metric observation and the terminal signoff timestamps for every section.
